ags": ["colloquial", "countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["It’s a jungle out there."], "quotes": [{"text": "'How do you like this corner of the jungle?' He leant forward. 'Just listen in to the couple behind you. From what I've heard they're straight out of \"Nigger Heaven\".'", "reference": "1954, Ian Fleming, “Nigger Heaven”, in Live and Let Die, London: Pan Books, published 1957, page 46:"}, {"text": "The first-timer just doesn't know what's going on when he gets to jail. […] It's a jungle, you've got to look after yourself first.", "reference": "1984, Barry Ellem, Doing Time, page 25:"}, {"text": "But of course, that excludes the narcissistic delusionals, the deliberate frauds, and the pathological cases of multiple personality. They are all out there in New Age Land, and it's a jungle!", "reference": "2005, Laura Knight-Jadczyk, The High Strangeness of Dimensions, Densities, and the Process of Alien Abduction:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(figurative) A tangled mess.", "tags": ["countable", "figuratively", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[…] lost in such a jungle of intrigues, pettifoggings, treacheries, diplomacies domestic and foreign […]", "reference": "1858–1865, Thomas Carlyle, History of Friedrich II. of Prussia, Called Frederick the Great, volume (please specify |volume=I to VI), London: Chapman and Hall, […], →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(slang) An area where hobos camp together.", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(music, uncountable) A style of electronic dance music and precursor of drum and bass.", "tags": ["uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Always more multiracial than other post-Rave scenes, Hardcore got “blacker” as hiphop, Ragga, dub and Soul influences kicked in, and by 93 it had evolved into Jungle. By this point, Hardcore/Jungle (the terms remain interchangeable) was universally scorned by dance hipsters and banished from the media.", "reference": "1994 September, Simon Reynolds, “Above The Treeline”, in The Wire:"}, {"text": "In large part, happycore was the result of an exodus of white ravers from the jungle scene, in reaction to the influx of black youth and the attendant mood change from bonhomie to surliness.", "reference": "2013, Simon Reynolds, Generation Ecstasy: Into the World of Techno and Rave Culture, page 291:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(golf slang) Dense rough.", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Hitting from the Jungle. The rough at some courses is just weeds and sparse grass, as often as not giving a player a decent lie to shoot from. But grass above four inches is nasty. It will grab your club and alter your shots.", "reference": "2006, Rob Blumer, Rex Chaney, Essential golf instruction, page 167:"}], "synonyms": ["tiger country"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(vulgar slang) A dense mass of pubic hair.", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable", "vulgar"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adjective", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈd͡ʒʌŋ.ɡ(ə)l/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "jangal", "tags": ["alternative", "dated"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle.", "tags": ["not comparable", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "She gave her first performance at the Philharmonic Auditorium in Los Angeles, offering festival dances, Moro tribal rituals, primitive jungle rhythms and rice harvest ceremonials.", "reference": "1939 January 8, The Tribune, Manila, page 13, column 2:"}, {"text": "Somewhere further up the valley a bunch of hippies were getting back to nature by loading up on mind altering chemicals and overwhelming their senses with five million decibels of digital bass and jungle beats.", "reference": "2005, Sean Dooley, The Big Twitch, Sydney: Allen and Unwin, page 9:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "selvático"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}